<title>ZIMBABWE: Finhold raises yr shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Finhold raises yr shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>	    (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			 141.65   vs   206.18</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			    --    vs   64.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income		    53.3   vs   81.3</p>
<p>    Taxation			    17.8   vs   29.7</p>
<p>    After-tax income		  35.5   vs   51.6</p>
<p>    Net trading income	     218.0   vs   169.5</p>
<p>Full name: Zimbabwe Financial Holdings Limited</p>
<p>NOTE:- The group said to strengthen its Zimbabwe Banking Corporation's capital adequacy, the central Reserve Bank would temporarily take up new capital in the commercial bank.</p>
<p>The group would issue 16 million convertible preference shares of Z$1 each to the central Reserve Bank of Zimbabwe at par for cash, a move which would dilute Finhold's interest in Zimbank. It said details of the transaction would be given soon.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9----</p>
